#%PAM-1.0
# PAM configuration for swaywardlock (the default `auth { pam service="swaywardlock"; }`).
# Install as /etc/pam.d/swaywardlock; swaywardlock refuses to lock without it.
# Only the auth phase runs (pam_authenticate, then pam_setcred to refresh credentials), as with
# swaylock and hyprlock: account policy such as pam_nologin or password expiry governs new
# logins and must not refuse the right password at the lock screen of a running session.
auth     include login
